# Booking attendance marking

## Scope

Minimum **DP-7** slice: operator marks **approved** registrations as **present** or **absent** on tour day. Registration lifecycle status stays `approved`; attendance is a separate projection on `operator_registrations`.

Not in scope: post-tour settlement, driver pay, carried-passenger accounting.

## Command

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| HTTP | `POST /bookings/:id/attendance` |
| Auth | Operator session — `admin` or `owner` (`assertOpsAccess`) |
| Body | `{ "attendanceStatus": "present" \| "absent" }` |
| Idempotency | Same status on same booking → `200` with existing row; no duplicate outbox |
| Conflict | Different status after mark → `409 BOOKING_ATTENDANCE_CONFLICT` |
| Gate | Registration `status` must be `approved` else `409 BOOKING_ATTENDANCE_INVALID_STATUS` |

## Persistence

Columns on `operator_registrations`:

- `attendance_status` — `present` \| `absent`
- `attendance_marked_at` — timestamptz
- `attendance_marked_by_user_id` — operator actor

## Outbox (SDE-001)

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| aggregateType | `registration` |
| aggregateId | booking id |
| eventType | `attendance.marked` (canonical) |
| domainEventId | `attendance.marked:{bookingId}:{markedAt ISO}` |
| payload | `bookingId`, `registrationId`, `tourId`, `submittedByUserId`, `guestUserId`, `attendanceStatus`, `markedAt`, `actorUserId` |

Relay invokes `dispatchMemberNotificationFromOutbox` → `member_notifications` inbox row with template `booking.attendance.marked`.

### Integration proof (MNI-001)

| Layer | Proof |
| ----- | ----- |
| Postgres | `pnpm --filter @apps/api run test:booking-attendance-postgres` — ATT-01..10 |
| Portal browser | `MNI-BRW-05` in `shared-notification-journeys-browser.spec.ts` — attendance → outbox → relay → inbox → mark-read |
| Operator UI | `operator-booking-attendance.spec.ts` — ATT-B01/B02 desktop/mobile RTL |

Chain: operator mark → durable outbox `attendance.marked` → relay → exactly one `member_notifications` row → portal inbox → mark-read persists after reload.

## Audit

Append-only `audit_events` row in same TX:

- action: `BOOKING_ATTENDANCE_MARKED`
- entityType: `registration`
- entityId: booking id
- metadata allowlist: `attendanceStatus`, `markedAt`

## Tenant isolation

All reads/writes under `withTenantRls(tenantId)`. Cross-tenant booking id → `404 BOOKING_NOT_FOUND`.

## Tests

- Postgres: command → outbox durable → relay → inbox (real Prisma)
- Playwright: operator UI present/absent on approved roster; FA RTL viewport; axe on action chrome
